 study of urban, suburban, rural differences</article-title><source>J Rheumatol</source><year>1994</year><volume>21</volume><fpage>302</fpage><lpage>306</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8182641</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Silman</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Hochberg</surname><given-names>MC</given-names></name></person-group><source>Epidemiology of the Rheumatic Diseases</source><year>2001</year><edition>2</edition><publisher-name>New York: Oxford University Press</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kim</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Neubert</surname><given-names>JK</given-names></name><name><surname>San Miguel</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Xu</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Krishnaraju</surname><given-names>RK</given-names></name><name><surname>Iadarola</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Goldman</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Dionne</surname><given-names>RA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Genetic influence on variability in human acute experimental pain sensitivity associated with gender, ethnicity and psychological temperament</article-title><source>Pain</source><year>2004</year><volume>109</volume><fpage>488</fpage><lpage>496</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15157710</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.pain.2004.02.027</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Diatchenko</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Slade</surname><given-names>GD</given-names></name><name><surname>Nackley</surname><given-names>AG</given-names></name><name><surname>Bhalang</surname><given-names>K</g